Modifications by CoworkOS contributors:
- Extracted only these 33 functions; no upstream Agent, environment, loader,
  generated wrappers, or unrelated tools are imported or distributed.
- Removed file writes, output-directory creation, plotting and global plotting
  configuration. Scalar functions use the Python standard library; NumPy and
  SciPy are imported lazily for the selected numerical analysis functions.
- Used the exact SI photon constants. Preserved the upstream default gas
  constant (8.31446261815324) for ideal-gas functions and 8.314 for the
  Clausius-Clapeyron approximation.
- Added explicit argument/finite-number/domain/size validation, fixed function
  dispatch and result envelopes containing units and model assumptions.
- Restricted ideal-gas arguments to scalars, sound addition to the exact
  logarithmic formula, propagation to the free-field point-source model,
  and phase changes to positive constant vaporization/sublimation enthalpy.
- Used stable logarithmic arithmetic for pressure ratios and sound addition;
  reject nonpositive temperature solutions and unrepresentable results.
- Normalized and serialized spectrum outputs; require a strictly increasing
  positive wavelength axis and nonnegative intensity with positive maximum;
  limit inputs to 8192 samples and results to 1024 peaks. Widths are null when
  not calculated, rather than the upstream zero-filled placeholder.
- Restricted baseline correction to polynomial detrending of sample indices,
  with bounded degree; excluded dense ALS and simplified rubberband modes.
  Return both the fitted trend and corrected signal without producing files.
- Kept raw-value peak detection separate from normalized spectrum analysis.
  Validate coordinates and return half-prominence widths in sample points,
  rather than describing every width as full width at half maximum.
- Restricted calibration to ordinary least-squares linear fitting with an
  intercept. Removed Python callable output and the unvalidated detection-limit
  estimate, and added bounded numeric predictions instead. R-squared is null
  for constant responses; nonlinear and custom models remain unavailable.
- Implemented standardized PCA with NumPy, without importing scikit-learn or
  pandas. Return numeric scores, loadings, variance, means and scales instead
  of estimator objects. Bound matrix shape, total cells and component count.
  Center in offset coordinates for stable population-standard-deviation scaling
  and centered training scores when feature values have large absolute offsets.
  Return centering_origin and centering_offset for stable reuse as
  (x - centering_origin) - centering_offset; means remains a rounded summary.
- Corrected Nernst reduction-potential sign for Ox + n e- -> Red:
  E = E0 + (R*T/(n*F))*ln(a_oxidized/a_reduced). The upstream implementation
  used the opposite sign with these argument names. Require dimensionless
  positive activities and preserve the input electrode reference.
- Extracted only first-order Bragg spacing from the selected XRD module;
  inputs are 2-theta in degrees and wavelength in angstrom, output angstrom.
  No crystallography package, Materials Project query or plotting is used.
- Extracted astronomy arithmetic into standard-library functions, without
  importing Astropy, Astroquery, NumPy or plotting modules. Retained explicit
  constants c = 299792458 m/s, G = 6.67430e-11 m^3/(kg s^2),
  R_sun = 6.957e8 m, L_sun = 3.828e26 W and sigma = 5.670374419e-8 W/(m^2 K^4).
- Bounded reddening, extinction, magnitude, radius and temperature inputs.
  Kept the modulus interval -10 to 30 mag and corrected the upstream prose:
  this corresponds to 0.1 to 10000000 pc, not the stated upper 100 kpc.
  Distance modulus is extinction-corrected and requires matching bands.
- Restricted stellar radii to solar units. Return bolometric luminosity in
  both nominal solar units and watts with converted radius and temperature.
  For transits retain remaining system luminosity and explicitly return depth
  fraction/percent, blocked area, luminosity lost and pre-transit total light.
  Both radii use solar units; the model is uniform brightness and full overlap
  with an unocculted companion, without limb darkening or a time-dependent curve.
  Star and companion light share a band (or both are bolometric), distance and
  solar-luminosity normalization so the luminosity ratio models observed flux.
- Restricted first-order Doppler conversion to abs(delta_lambda/lambda_0)
  <= 0.001, with signed velocity and matching wavelength conventions.
  Use stable arithmetic for Kepler period and specify the Newtonian,
  weak-field, negligible-companion-mass approximation. Explicitly define the
  binary mass ratio as m1/m2 = k2/k1 from positive fitted semi-amplitudes.
- Preserved the original 12-function catalog for v1-pinned Runs and the
  18-function catalog for v2-pinned Runs. The expanded 26-function catalog is
  a separate v3 selection.
- Added only cubic lattice parameter, direct metric tensor, general plane
  spacing and Scherrer estimates from the selected materials modules. Replaced
  their NumPy matrix operations with bounded standard-library arithmetic.
  Validate integer nonzero Miller triples, symmetric 3x3 positive-definite
  metrics and conditioning; reject invalid and nearly degenerate cells.
  Return the direct metric in square angstrom and cell volume in cubic angstrom;
  reciprocal metric conventions exclude a 2-pi factor and spacings use angstrom.
- Changed Scherrer instrumental correction from direct subtraction with an
  unspecified profile to explicit Gaussian quadrature:
  beta = sqrt((observed_FWHM - instrumental_FWHM) *
              (observed_FWHM + instrumental_FWHM)), with both widths on the
  2-theta degree axis before conversion to radians. Reject nearly cancelling
  corrected widths. Return D_nm and intermediate values with explicit units.
  D estimates coherent diffraction-domain size, not measured particle/grain
  size; no strain separation, profile fit or Lorentzian/Voigt deconvolution.
- Preserved v1-v4 catalog entries and implementations. The v5 selection has
  33 tools: these 30 upstream adaptations and three native RDKit wrappers.
- Normalize mass-spectrum centroid intensities to the input base peak as 100
  before inclusive relative-threshold filtering. Return raw and relative
  intensities, base_peak and highest_mz_peak, removing the unsupported upstream
  assignment of the highest-m/z peak as molecular_ion. Bound centroid inputs
  to 8192 and retained outputs to 1024, rejecting excess instead of truncating.
- Make num_carbon actually contribute to the isotope pattern. Convolve
  independent chlorine/carbon binomials into nominal shifts j+2*k using fixed
  Cl37=0.2424 and C13=0.0107, recording these isotope fractions. Preserve all
  bins, including zeros, and distinguish probabilities from base-100 relative
  intensities. Exclude other elements, enrichment and exact-mass fine structure.
- Find nominal M/M+2/M+4/M+6 candidates at a supplied absolute charge using
  2/abs_charge spacing, anchoring later windows to the observed M centroid.
  Use bounded inclusive tolerance windows; reject multiple candidates rather
  than silently choosing the first. Preserve requested/observed anchors,
  deviations and missing labels; undefined M+2/M ratios remain null.
  No chloride count, charge, molecular-ion, fragment or structure inference.
- The v6 selection preserves v1-v5 and has 37 tools: these 33 upstream
  adaptations and four native RDKit wrappers. The mass-spectrum functions use
  only the Python standard library; no new scientific dependency is installed.

