The later v4 catalog also contains three CoworkOS-native RDKit wrappers in
src/tools/science/chemistry.py. They are not part of these 33 upstream
adaptations and contain no copied SciAgentGYM or RDKit source. Their provenance
is atria-native; their implementation remains MIT. RDKit is an optional,
user-managed external dependency under its own BSD-3-Clause license, not a
bundled SciAgentGYM component. See the repository's THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

The v6 rdkit_exact_mass_and_formula wrapper in
src/tools/science/mass-chemistry.py is also new CoworkOS MIT code, not an extracted
SciAgentGYM molecular-properties function. It reuses the unchanged v4 input
parser and public RDKit ExactMolWt/CalcMolFormula APIs in the user-selected
environment. Formula output preserves explicit isotopes; mass uses Da and
zero net formal charge. It does not calculate ion/adduct m/z, DBE, fragments,
structural rankings or molecular-ion identity. RDKit remains external BSD-3-Clause.
